# PR merge gate (agent checklist)

Lesson [#83](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/pull/83): do **not** merge with unresolved actionable bot threads.

**SSOT detail:** `CONTRIBUTING.md` → “Review check before merge”. This file is the short agent checklist only.

## Trap

**CI soft-pass ≠ a code review.** Try to get one CodeRabbit review from GitHub or the local CLI / IDE. Do not wait more than 10 minutes for either review surface: if one is rate-limited beyond that, use the other if it can review sooner. If neither can complete a review, the main agent still reviews the diff and records the rate-limit outcome in a one-line PR note. Soft-pass ≠ on-demand/label skip.

## Jev recommendation during implementation

Follow `AGENTS.md` → “Jev-guided workflow” at meaningful loop boundaries. Jev does not review code and cannot waive the ready-PR CodeRabbit gate below.

## Decision table (gate 1 — CodeRabbit on HEAD)

This gate governs merging a ready PR, not implementation progress. If CodeRabbit is missing, pending, or rate-limited, continue coding, run checks, update the draft PR, and prepare the change. Only hold the merge action under the conditions below.

| Situation | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Draft PR | CR completeness not required; still fail on unresolved bot threads. Do not merge drafts. |
| Ready + missing / pending / error / on-demand skip | **HOLD** — `@coderabbitai full review` (or label). Undraft alone does not request. |
| Ready + after fix commits | `@coderabbitai review` (incremental) |
| GitHub `Review completed` on current HEAD | Review gate satisfied; avoid redundant local review by default |
| Local CodeRabbit review completed on current diff | Review gate satisfied when GitHub is rate-limited beyond 10m; record the GitHub reset and local review in a one-line PR note |
| A rate-limited surface reports reset **≤10m** | **HOLD** until the reset, then retry. If the request becomes pending, let it complete regardless of elapsed time |
| A surface reports reset **>10m** | That review is not required; try the other surface and proceed after main-agent review if neither can complete |
| Review is pending / in progress | **HOLD** until it completes; the 10-minute limit applies only to rate limiting |
| All available review surfaces are rate-limited beyond 10m | Main-agent review is required; record the attempts and reset information in a one-line PR note, then proceed |
| Unresolved actionable bot threads | **HOLD** unless user `rmw` / `rmcw` / `--waive` / label |

## Before merge (ordered)

1. PR **ready** (not draft).
2. Try for one CodeRabbit review on the current diff using GitHub or local CLI / IDE. If a review is pending or in progress, wait for it to complete; the 10-minute limit applies only to a rate-limited surface.
3. `./scripts/check_pr_reviews.sh` (or with PR number).
4. Disposition **every** actionable finding (threads + outside-diff/summary) — see `coderabbit-lessons.mdc`.
5. For a rate-limit reset of 10 minutes or less, wait for the reset and retry. If all available review surfaces are rate-limited beyond 10 minutes, complete main-agent diff review and document the attempts / resets in a one-line PR note; re-run the script after fixes. A pending review remains a hold until it completes, regardless of elapsed time.
6. User shorthand: `rm`/`rmc` = merge after the available review path and checks; `rmw`/`rmcw` = waiver for other holds; `all rmc` = loop open drafts.

## Layers (one-liner)

Local while iterating → GitHub when merge-candidate → `./scripts/check_pr_reviews.sh` + CI **Bot review threads** (status `unresolved bot threads`).
